# Word list for vim's spell checker.  config_vim.sh links this in as
# ~/.vim/spell/en.utf-8.add, which is the 'spellfile' _vimrc sets, and
# compiles it with :mkspell!.  vim reads only the compiled .add.spl and
# rebuilds it by itself just for zg and zw, so a word added by hand here
# needs config_vim.sh re-run before vim sees it.  zg appends through the
# symlink, so words added while editing land in this file.
#
# One word per line.  Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# the markers AutoSpellGoodWords searches a buffer for
SpellGoodWordsStart
SpellGoodWordsEnd

